  "about": "Every drawn display reference image (#571): its file and the renderer inputs that make it. test/ref/make_refs.sh renders them all with jog-reference, and the Kit's DisplayFirmwareReferenceTests checks every one against the renderer now, from this one list. deck, color [r, g, b] and player (a Syndicate player type, or null for none) make the deck; stale draws the waiting look; title, artist, key and bpm are its text; beat (1-4), needle (0-16383, op 09's scale), meter [level, peak] (0-127), phase (1/16384 beats, op 0B's scale), time [elapsed, length] in seconds and look (red or white, the warning's) are the live parts. Each is JogDisplayRenderer.drawnImage cropped to the 198 frame, or with canvas 216 the whole drawn image.",
